{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And shall make atonement for himself.</b> This is confession of words. Could it be atonement through blood? I would reason: atonement through a bull is stated here, and atonement through a goat is stated below — לכפר עליו. Just as the atonement stated regarding the goat is confession of words apart from the blood, as it is written והתודה עליו, so too the atonement stated here regarding the bull is confession of words apart from the blood. And if you ask: why does he not confess over the inner goat — one of the three confessions? One may answer: since it is for Above, as it is written עלה עליו הגורל לה׳, it would be a disgrace vis-à-vis below to confess over it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:38.635367109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}